kepler-formal: name the problem in the solver's start and finish lines

"Starting solver" said nothing about what the solver was given, and a
solve that ran for half an hour on a 256 x 64, 21-port register file
could not be told apart from a hang or judged against a smaller one.
The two existing lines now carry it, adding no lines to the log:

  Starting solver: <variables> variables, <clauses> clauses, <n> outputs compared
  SAT solver finished: UNSAT in <seconds> s

SATSolverWrapper counts the clauses it is handed and the largest
variable they use.

Not upstreamed; carried by bazel-orfs (MODULE.bazel, kepler-formal's
git_override). Retires at a bump onto a kepler-formal that logs the
problem size itself.

diff --git a/src/sat/SATSolverWrapper.h b/src/sat/SATSolverWrapper.h
index a024dec..52748ef 100644
--- a/src/sat/SATSolverWrapper.h
+++ b/src/sat/SATSolverWrapper.h
@@ -340,9 +340,19 @@ public:
     addClauseRange(lits);
   }
 
+  // The problem as handed to the solver, for the log line that starts it:
+  // clauses added and the largest variable any of them uses.
+  size_t numClauses() const { return numClauses_; }
+  size_t numVariables() const { return numVariables_; }
+
  private:
   template <typename ClauseRange>
   void addClauseRange(const ClauseRange& lits) {
+    ++numClauses_;
+    for (int lit : lits) {
+      // external +-(var+2): a literal of magnitude v is variable v-1 counted from 1
+      numVariables_ = std::max(numVariables_, static_cast<size_t>(std::abs(lit)) - 1);
+    }
     if (solverType_ == KEPLER_FORMAL::Config::SolverType::GLUCOSE) {
       Glucose::vec<Glucose::Lit> clause;
       for (int lit : lits) {
@@ -1115,6 +1125,8 @@ public:
